cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite the Polygon Mesh Processing Library.
title: PMP (Polygon Mesh Processing Library) subset for curvenet.elf (vendored)
abstract: >-
  The pmp-library as the org's Godot fork carries it under thirdparty/pmp
  (the pin cassie-triangulation uses, f2fb04f4, with the fork's
  -fno-exceptions patches). Subset: core (surface_mesh) and the algorithms
  remeshing, decimation, differential_geometry, normals, features,
  utilities, distance_point_triangle and triangulation, with the headers
  they include (barycentric_coordinates.h, io/io_flags.h, ...). Not
  vendored: curvature, laplace, numerics, smoothing and the other Eigen
  users. 9 sources, 16 headers and LICENSE.txt, 256,850 bytes before this
  file. Built with PMP_SCALAR_TYPE_64=1 (pmp::Point is double).
  tools/vendor/thirdparty_subset.sh reproduces the tree from the pinned
  commit. Local adaptations (tools/vendor/patches/pmp.patch), both behind
  PMP_NO_EIGEN so curvenet.elf is Eigen-free: mat_vec.h drops the
  <Eigen/Dense> include and the Matrix construct-from/assign-from/cast-to
  Eigen members; remeshing.cpp drops the curvature.h include and the
  adaptive-sizing block of preprocessing() (adaptive_remeshing aborts with
  a message; uniform_remeshing, the path Cassie uses, is unchanged).
  And, unconditionally: tangential_smoothing falls back to
  weighted_centroid when minimize_squared_areas' 3x3 system is singular,
  as upstream's catch of the SolverException did; the fork's
  -fno-exceptions patch had made that an abort, which every planar patch
  hits (a flat one-ring's squared-area matrix has rank 2; Gate 4: an
  8-point planar circle aborted CassieTriangulator in refine_patch).
type: software
authors:
